{"kind":"artifact","text":"Design note for a second application at notes/2026-08-13-second-application.md on exact head e5b39b65fbd8e74762ed5764d329ad74990a2e61. It decides: one repository one application, bound at init by a signed record naming the application by pinned commit hash (URL as provenance, fold-profile hash included); an application is an ordinary Git repository, a Go module importing the kernel, published as releases or source-only and installed by pointing at it anywhere; install authorizes interpretation never execution, with honest degradation to kernel-verifiable-but-uninterpretable when the host lacks the declared interpreter; legacy repositories without a binding default to Workroom. Chess is the worked example, in its own repository as the first external importer of the public kernel API, with a rules-engine fold that judges illegal moves ineffective and computes checkmate as a projection fact. Self-initiated design work resting on the ratified fold-purity decision.","body":{"commit":"e5b39b65fbd8e74762ed5764d329ad74990a2e61","path":"notes/2026-08-13-second-application.md"}}